## 4.4. Preparation of HKUST-1 metal-organic framework
HKUST-1 was synthesised by immersing two Cu foil electrodes $(\sim16\mathrm{cm}^{2})$ ), approximately $2\mathrm{cm}$ apart, into a 1:1 ethanol:deionised water solution containing $48\mathrm{mM}$ 1,3,5 – benzenetricarboxylic acid linker and $64\mathrm{mM}$ methyltributylammonium methyl sulphate supporting electrolyte.45 The solution was maintained at $55~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and deaerated with $\Nu_{2}$ (g) whilst a PGSTAT302N potentiostat (Metrohm Autolab B.V., The Netherlands) was used to apply a fixed potential difference of $2.5\mathrm{~V~}$ between the two $\mathrm{Cu}$ foil electrodes for one hour. This generated HKUST-1 in solution which was collected by centrifugation. The HKUST-1 was then re-suspended in methanol,
